[225.0457, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## PAY-381 operations\n\nWebhook deliveries always require a fresh, valid `Paygate-Signature`; a replay-token\nheader does not bypass signature verification. Failed stored events can be retried\nthrough the permission-checked internal replay API, or trusted local backlog files\ncan be re-driven with `npm run replay-backlog`.\n\nBacklog replay preserves the payments on-call refund-storm guard (20 events per run,\n120 seconds between runs). Run subsequent batches after the cooldown until no events\nremain. Processed event IDs persist in `DATA_DIR`, so retries do not create another\nrefund or audit entry. Keep the same data directory when restarting or replaying.\n\nRefunds in INR up to and including 500000 paise (₹5,000) are auto-approved; larger\nrefunds and other currencies go to manual review.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('test/pay381.test.ts'); s=p.read_text()\nneedle='  assert.equal(store.listRefunds().length, 1);\\n});\\n'\npos=s.rfind(needle)\nassert pos != -1\ns=s[:pos]+'''  assert.equal(store.listRefunds().length, 1);\n  // Failed but authenticated events remain recoverable through the internal API.\n  store.saveRawEvent(\"evt_failed\", JSON.stringify(event(\"evt_failed\", \"refund.requested\", { refund_id: \"rf_recovered\" })));\n  const recovered = await fetch(`${base}/admin/replay/evt_failed`, {\n    method: \"POST\", headers: { authorization: \"Bearer ops-key\" },\n  });\n  assert.equal(recovered.status, 200);\n  assert.deepEqual(await recovered.json(), { replayed: true, outcome: \"processed\" });\n  assert.equal(store.isProcessed(\"evt_failed\"), true);\n  assert.equal(store.listRefunds().length, 2);\n  const recoveredBefore = snapshot(dir);\n  assert.equal((await fetch(`${base}/admin/replay/evt_failed`, {\n    method: \"POST\", headers: { authorization: \"Bearer ops-key\" },\n  })).status, 409);\n  assert.deepEqual(snapshot(dir), recoveredBefore);\n});\n''' + s[pos+len(needle):]\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nnpm test; git --no-pager diff --check; git --no-pager diff --stat\n"]
[225.046578, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[225.047605, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[225.048052, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ## PAY-381 operations\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Webhook deliveries always require a fresh, valid `Paygate-Signature`; a replay-token\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> header does not bypass signature verification. Failed stored events can be retried\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> through the permission-checked internal replay API, or trusted local backlog files\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> can be re-driven with `npm run replay-backlog`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Backlog replay preserves the payments on-call refund-storm guard (20 events per run,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 120 seconds between runs). Run subsequent batches after the cooldown until no events\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> remain. Processed event IDs persist in `DATA_DIR`, so retries do not create another\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> refund or audit entry. Keep the same data directory when restarting or replaying.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Refunds in INR up to and including 500000 paise (₹5,000) are auto-approved; larger\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> refunds and other currencies go to manual review.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
